From 62a56e350fcfd1c5e204c62dac4ea4ee205eb24e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/vc4: hdmi: Reset the MAI FIFO when preparing audio

The MAI FIFO is only reset, and its DLATE/error flags cleared, in
vc4_hdmi_audio_startup, which runs when the PCM is opened. Recovery
from an xrun (and a stop/prepare/start by e.g. PipeWire) only calls
prepare, so the FIFO is restarted without being reset.

After an underrun this leaves DLATE set and the multichannel audio
shifted by half a frame: on an 8 channel stream FL/FR carry RL/RR and
so on, until the device is closed and reopened.

Reset and flush the FIFO and clear the status flags in prepare too.

Checked with an HDMI analyser, 8 channels at 48kHz and 192kHz, with
forced underruns: without this every run is rotated by 4 channels,
with it the channel order is correct.

Link: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/issues/7750
Signed-off-by: Dom Cobley <popcornmix@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
@@ -2070,6 +2070,13 @@ static int vc4_hdmi_audio_prepare(struct
 	vc4_hdmi_audio_set_mai_clock(vc4_hdmi, sample_rate);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&vc4_hdmi->hw_lock, flags);
+	/* Also reached on xrun recovery, where startup is not called */
+	HDMI_WRITE(HDMI_MAI_CTL,
+		   VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_RESET |
+		   VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_FLUSH |
+		   VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_DLATE |
+		   VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_ERRORE |
+		   VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_ERRORF);
 	HDMI_WRITE(HDMI_MAI_CTL,
 		   VC4_SET_FIELD(channels, VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_CHNUM) |
 		   VC4_HD_MAI_CTL_WHOLSMP |
